    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "AIDS",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "Peripheral neuropathy, a potential side effect of many anti-HIV therapies and HIV itself, can adversely affect quality of life. The most effective management of peripheral neuropathy starts with identifying the cause, such as the use of certain HIV drugs, alcohol drinking, and deficiencies of vitamins B12 and E. Persons suffering from peripheral neuropathy should first determine if any common causes are present. If the cause cannot be determined, then pain management is required, and the treatment choice is determined by symptom severity. Suggestions for treating pain based on severity of symptoms are highlighted. Also included are treatment suggestions for severe and prolonged pain, including not wearing tight-fitting socks, being ambulatory, acupuncture, and deep tissue massage."
    }
